Interesting - the commit `475f6d25c` is not in the history of our HEAD. Let me check if the fix is present in the current code. Looking at the current `tt_face_palette_set` in ttcpal.c, I can see it does NOT have the bounds check for `color_index + num_palette_entries > num_colors`. So the vulnerability is present.

Let me also check the `tt_face_load_colr_layers` for the missing bounds check on `first_layer_index + num_layers`:

Looking at the current code in `tt_face_load_colr_layers`:
```c
layer_record_ptr = colr->layers +
                   glyph_record.first_layer_index * LAYER_SIZE;

if ( FT_NEW_ARRAY( layers, glyph_record.num_layers ) )
  goto Error;

for ( layer_idx = 0; layer_idx < glyph_record.num_layers; layer_idx++ )
{
  FT_UShort  gid                 = FT_NEXT_USHORT( layer_record_ptr );
  FT_UShort  palette_entry_index = FT_NEXT_USHORT( layer_record_ptr );
  ...
}
```

There's no check that `first_layer_index + num_layers <= num_layers`. This is the vulnerability.

